    "question_text": "William wants to cook roast beef and potatoes for himself and four friends. From his cookbook he gets the following information: BEEF Medium oven Hot oven Rare --- 10 minutes per 500 g Medium rare 20 minutes per 500 g plus 20 mins 15 minutes per 500 g plus 15 minutes Well done 30 minutes per 500 g plus 30 minutes --- Allow 300 g per person. After removing from the oven, the meat should be allowed to stand for 10 minutes. ROAST POTATOES Medium oven Hot oven 40 minutes 30 minutes William buys a joint of the correct weight and decides to cook it medium rare in a hot oven. How long after putting the beef in the oven should he put in the potatoes, so that both will be ready to serve at the same time?",
